WEBVTT


00:00:43.973 --> 00:00:46.066
[THUNDER RUMBLING]


00:00:46.475 --> 00:00:48.443
[WOMAN CACKLING]


00:00:48.611 --> 00:00:50.340
FRED:
Come on.


00:00:54.416 --> 00:00:56.247
Split up.


00:00:59.955 --> 00:01:02.617
SHAGGY: Hey, come on, Scoob.
SCOOBY: I'm right behind you, Shaggy.


00:01:02.791 --> 00:01:04.884
[SHAGGY SCREAMS]


00:01:05.427 --> 00:01:07.588
Change of plans.


00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:13.492
WOMAN:
Stay out.


00:01:13.669 --> 00:01:15.762
[GRUNTING]


00:01:16.739 --> 00:01:19.902
Time to unmask the person
behind this mystery.


00:01:21.443 --> 00:01:24.241
- It's you?
- What?


00:01:24.413 --> 00:01:27.280
Like, it can't be.


00:01:37.893 --> 00:01:41.021
MAN: Remember, people, just because
this is the last day of class...


00:01:41.263 --> 00:01:43.288
...doesn't mean
this test doesn't count.


00:01:47.269 --> 00:01:48.497
Huh?


00:01:52.307 --> 00:01:54.036
No.


00:02:06.522 --> 00:02:07.682
Yes.


00:02:08.924 --> 00:02:11.051
Cowabunga.


00:02:15.564 --> 00:02:17.031
- Hot dog.
- Hot dog.


00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.502
GIRL 1:
Let's dance.


00:02:22.571 --> 00:02:24.436
Yeah.


00:02:36.852 --> 00:02:37.944
[GIRL 2 WHISTLES]


00:02:38.587 --> 00:02:42.216
Uh, guys, what are you doing?


00:02:42.458 --> 00:02:44.722
I know you're excited
the school year's over...


00:02:44.893 --> 00:02:46.952
...but our seasonal employment
awaits.


00:02:47.162 --> 00:02:50.563
Already? Like, I didn't even have time
to get a tan.


00:02:50.733 --> 00:02:52.496
- Yeah.
- Come on.


00:02:57.539 --> 00:02:59.598
[CHEERING]


00:03:03.545 --> 00:03:06.275
Well, it sure is lucky
that Daphne's uncle...


00:03:06.482 --> 00:03:09.076
...is opening his new country club
this summer, hey, V?


00:03:09.251 --> 00:03:12.379
Indeed. Without these summer jobs,
we'd never able to pay back...


00:03:12.554 --> 00:03:15.114
...Old Man Frickert
for the damage we did to his barn.


00:03:15.691 --> 00:03:17.716
Say cheese.


00:03:17.893 --> 00:03:19.224
[GIGGLES]


00:03:19.394 --> 00:03:22.090
- What is he--?
- Oh, Scoob's got a new hobby.


00:03:22.264 --> 00:03:23.731
Scrapbooking.


00:03:23.899 --> 00:03:27.130
- What happened to gardening?
- It didn't work out.


00:03:27.302 --> 00:03:30.499
Everything he planted,
he'd just dig right up.


00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.407
VELMA:
Hm.


00:03:33.809 --> 00:03:37.609
Daphne said we should hit the road
right after school.


00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.975
Any sign of her or Fred?


00:03:40.149 --> 00:03:41.707
Uh-uh.


00:03:42.785 --> 00:03:44.047
[VELMA GASPS]


00:03:44.219 --> 00:03:46.380
- Like, huh?
VELMA: Jinkies.


00:03:46.588 --> 00:03:48.055
Ooh.


00:03:48.791 --> 00:03:50.554
Perfect.


00:03:53.328 --> 00:03:56.991
Well? I for one think we deserve
an explanation.


00:03:57.166 --> 00:03:58.895
- Yeah.
- Yes.


00:03:59.101 --> 00:04:03.765
There's always been an undeniable
chemistry between you two, but--


00:04:03.939 --> 00:04:07.636
When did the transformative reaction
finally occur?


00:04:08.677 --> 00:04:11.168
I guess it started that night
at Old Man Frickert's.


00:04:11.346 --> 00:04:13.246
Yeah. Remember, Velma?


00:04:13.415 --> 00:04:17.010
We followed the trail of the vengeful
scarecrow up into the hayloft.


00:04:17.186 --> 00:04:19.120
This is impossible.


00:04:19.288 --> 00:04:21.813
We'll never find anything in here.


00:04:22.191 --> 00:04:24.853
Yes, if I wasn't so pun averse...


00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:28.188
...I might even say it's like looking
for a needle in a haystack.


00:04:28.363 --> 00:04:29.625
[MAN ROARS]


00:04:29.798 --> 00:04:31.698
MAN:
Didn't scare you, did I?


00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.367
[VELMA & DAPHNE SCREAMING]


00:04:33.569 --> 00:04:35.002
Daphne.


00:04:37.673 --> 00:04:39.334
Are you okay?


00:04:40.142 --> 00:04:42.110
I am now.


00:04:43.979 --> 00:04:46.277
SHAGGY: Like, run!
- What is it, Shaggy?


00:04:46.448 --> 00:04:49.781
- This one's gonna be a real barn burner.
FRED: Shaggy.


00:04:50.352 --> 00:04:52.115
Look out!


00:04:54.656 --> 00:04:57.318
DAPHNE: And thus,
we're stuck paying for a new barn.


00:04:57.492 --> 00:04:59.653
Again, just for the record...


00:04:59.828 --> 00:05:02.388
...nowhere on those bales of hay
did it say flammable.


00:05:02.598 --> 00:05:05.158
SCOOBY: Yeah.
- Anyway, that was also the night...


00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:08.462
...that Fred and I realized
we were just meant to be.


00:05:11.874 --> 00:05:13.967
It's a lovely story.


00:05:14.142 --> 00:05:17.077
But I do feel obligated
to raise one concern.


00:05:17.246 --> 00:05:19.407
Whenever there's a shift
in a relationship...


00:05:19.615 --> 00:05:22.311
...between two individuals
within a group...


00:05:22.484 --> 00:05:26.181
...it inevitably has repercussions
on the group as a whole.


00:05:27.489 --> 00:05:30.322
SHAGGY:
Oh, Velma, don't worry about that.


00:05:30.492 --> 00:05:33.325
We're all way too mature
to let that happen.


00:05:33.495 --> 00:05:36.487
- Right, Scoob?
- I know I am.


00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.433
Punch buggy white.


00:05:39.635 --> 00:05:43.071
Ouch. Oh, good one, Scoob.


00:05:43.238 --> 00:05:46.605
But it's a shame you didn't notice
the punch buggy green.


00:05:46.775 --> 00:05:48.208
Ow!


00:05:50.145 --> 00:05:51.737
[SHAGGY & SCOOBY GRUNTING]


00:05:51.914 --> 00:05:54.405
- All right.
- You know what? That is it. I've had it.


00:05:54.583 --> 00:05:58.019
You know, I will turn this van around.


00:05:59.421 --> 00:06:01.582
- Do I have to come back there?
DAPHNE: Scooby-Doo...


00:06:01.757 --> 00:06:04.157
...get your tail out of my face.


00:06:05.394 --> 00:06:08.192
DAPHNE: Fred, where are those
directions I sent you to print out?


00:06:08.397 --> 00:06:12.197
Don't worry, we're not lost.


00:06:17.773 --> 00:06:21.300
DAPHNE: Hm. This sure doesn't look
like my uncle's country club.


00:06:22.444 --> 00:06:25.311
Oh. Hey, look. It's the S.S. Daphne.


00:06:26.381 --> 00:06:28.281
DAPHNE:
Ha, ha.


00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.975
Oh, look. Try stopping there, sweetie.


00:06:31.219 --> 00:06:33.414
FRED:
Whatever you say, dear.


00:06:42.264 --> 00:06:44.596
VELMA:
Oh, how quaint.


00:06:54.609 --> 00:06:55.633
Hm.


00:06:55.811 --> 00:06:57.802
Hello?


00:06:58.013 --> 00:07:00.243
Anybody home?


00:07:00.449 --> 00:07:03.748
Like, yikes. Maybe we ought to just find
our own way...


00:07:03.919 --> 00:07:06.012
...to your uncle's country club.


00:07:07.289 --> 00:07:08.313
Zoinks!


00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:09.684
Country club?


00:07:09.858 --> 00:07:12.952
You're going to the country club?


00:07:13.128 --> 00:07:15.028
Yes, we have summer jobs there.


00:07:15.263 --> 00:07:19.529
No, you must turn back.
You must leave while you still can.


00:07:19.735 --> 00:07:23.694
- Leave? Why would we wanna leave?
- They were fools to build there.


00:07:23.872 --> 00:07:25.032
I tried to warn them...


00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:27.640
...but they thought
I was just some crazy hag.


00:07:27.809 --> 00:07:30.107
You? Heh. No.


00:07:30.312 --> 00:07:34.510
But mark my words,
the lake monster will return.


00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:38.743
The lake monster will return.


00:07:39.755 --> 00:07:41.814
[WHIMPERING]


00:07:42.524 --> 00:07:44.617
- Did you get directions?
- Uh....


00:07:44.793 --> 00:07:46.693
- Not exactly.
SHAGGY: Oh, yes, we did.


00:07:46.895 --> 00:07:49.989
Make a U-turn
and head straight back to Coolsville.


00:07:50.198 --> 00:07:53.634
There's a monster at the lake, guys.
A monster.


00:07:53.835 --> 00:07:55.996
- A monster?
- Mm-hm.


00:07:56.204 --> 00:07:59.298
Would you be referring
to the lake monster of Erie Pointe?


00:07:59.875 --> 00:08:02.343
You know, I didn't catch his name.


00:08:02.511 --> 00:08:05.639
- All I heard was "monster."
VELMA: No, look.


00:08:07.382 --> 00:08:10.977
It says here for hundreds of years
there have been sightings...


00:08:11.153 --> 00:08:14.919
...of hideous creatures
said to live at the bottom of the lake.


00:08:15.157 --> 00:08:18.820
I get it, it's one of those things
like Bigfoot or the Loch Ness monster.


00:08:19.027 --> 00:08:22.155
Oh, no, it's worse than we thought.


00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:25.424
No, Shaggy, I think what Fred means
is that it's just a legend.


00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:29.001
You know, lots of small towns
make them up. They're good for tourism.


00:08:29.438 --> 00:08:32.601
Oh. Oh, sure, you know,
come for the scenery...


00:08:32.808 --> 00:08:35.208
...stay for the certain death.


00:08:35.844 --> 00:08:36.868
[THUD]


00:08:37.045 --> 00:08:39.707
Come on, guys. Let's just get going
or we're gonna be late.


00:08:41.883 --> 00:08:43.612
Uh, Fred?


00:08:44.319 --> 00:08:47.550
- We still don't know how to get there.
- Mm-hm.


00:08:47.722 --> 00:08:52.022
Actually, yes, we do.


00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:53.588
[SHAGGY SIGHS]


00:08:53.762 --> 00:08:55.229
- No.
- Yes.


00:09:07.542 --> 00:09:09.032
FRED:
Pretty swank, Daph.


00:09:09.211 --> 00:09:13.204
DAPHNE: Yeah, looks like my uncle
really outdid himself this time.


00:09:17.219 --> 00:09:18.982
Thanks, Shaggy.


00:09:19.554 --> 00:09:20.578
[LAUGHS]


00:09:20.755 --> 00:09:24.748
- Is that my favorite niece?
- Uncle Thorny.


00:09:26.428 --> 00:09:27.725
Wow.


00:09:29.131 --> 00:09:31.156
Thank you again, uncle.


00:09:31.366 --> 00:09:34.267
I don't know what we would've done
without these summer jobs.


00:09:34.436 --> 00:09:37.337
Yeah. And, again, just for the record...


00:09:37.506 --> 00:09:40.475
...it's a well-known fact
that scarecrows are afraid of fire--


00:09:40.642 --> 00:09:41.666
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:09:41.877 --> 00:09:44.903
Gang, I'd like you to meet
Thorton Blake IV.


00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.445
Fifth, actually.


00:09:46.615 --> 00:09:48.378
Uncle Thorny, this is the gang.


00:09:48.583 --> 00:09:49.607
This is Shaggy.


00:09:49.784 --> 00:09:50.944
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:09:51.119 --> 00:09:52.780
- Fred.
- Oh.


00:09:53.255 --> 00:09:54.654
DAPHNE: Velma.
- Pleasure.


00:09:54.823 --> 00:09:56.256
- And--
SCOOBY: Scooby-Doo.


00:09:56.424 --> 00:09:57.982
Nice to meet you, Uncle Thorny.


00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.025
Smile.


00:10:00.195 --> 00:10:01.890
[SCOOBY GIGGLES]


00:10:02.597 --> 00:10:05.828
Well, I'm sure glad to have you all
on board this summer.


00:10:06.034 --> 00:10:10.471
Grab your stuff, get settled,
and park that thing in the back.


00:10:10.639 --> 00:10:13.802
Oh. You're gonna need
to get a good night's sleep.


00:10:13.975 --> 00:10:17.638
Your shifts start at 6 a.m. sharp.


00:10:18.914 --> 00:10:20.609
There's a 6 a.m.?


00:10:21.650 --> 00:10:22.674
[SIGHS]


00:10:24.519 --> 00:10:27.352
And that one. It's my makeup.


00:10:30.525 --> 00:10:32.288
[SHAGGY GRUNTING]


00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:35.861
- Shaggy, need a hand?
- No, thanks, Fred. I got it.


00:10:36.031 --> 00:10:38.727
It just takes a little elbow grease.


00:10:38.934 --> 00:10:40.458
[GASPING]


00:10:40.635 --> 00:10:41.932
Shaggy.


00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:49.172
Shaggy, are you all right?


00:10:49.878 --> 00:10:52.346
Like, I am now.


00:10:53.248 --> 00:10:54.545
Shaggy.


00:10:55.317 --> 00:10:57.080
Yes, Velma?


00:10:57.319 --> 00:11:01.312
I don't know how much longer
I can hold you.


00:11:13.068 --> 00:11:15.093
- Hey, Scoob?
- Huh?


00:11:16.504 --> 00:11:19.268
- Can I talk to you man-to-man?
- Uh....


00:11:19.474 --> 00:11:21.499
Sort of.


00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:25.077
I think I might have just had
a hayloft moment with Velma.


00:11:26.281 --> 00:11:28.715
Do you think it's possible that--?


00:11:28.883 --> 00:11:34.753
I don't know,
that she and I are meant to be?


00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:37.717
[LAUGHING]


00:11:41.062 --> 00:11:43.758
Yeah. Thanks for the support, pal.


00:11:43.999 --> 00:11:46.695
I'll remember this come flea season.


00:11:49.104 --> 00:11:51.197
[PUFFING]


00:11:54.242 --> 00:11:56.301
[CONTINUES LAUGHING]


00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.417
[TREE BRANCHES RUSTLE]


00:12:04.252 --> 00:12:07.380
Getting much better distance
on those woods, sir.


00:12:08.089 --> 00:12:13.117
Hey, Fred,
can I talk to you man-to-man?


00:12:13.795 --> 00:12:15.456
Sort of.


00:12:16.064 --> 00:12:20.592
Well, you and Daphne,
is that something you recommend?


00:12:20.769 --> 00:12:22.396
What do you mean?


00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:25.130
Well, you know, going from having...


00:12:25.307 --> 00:12:28.970
...you know, a girl friend
to a girlfriend.


00:12:29.144 --> 00:12:33.410
Heh, heh. I don't know if I'd really
call Daphne my girlfriend, Shags.


00:12:33.581 --> 00:12:36.106
You know, it's more casual than that.
We're just, um....


00:12:36.284 --> 00:12:38.616
- We're hanging out.
- Hanging out?


00:12:38.787 --> 00:12:41.517
No, Fred is totally my boyfriend.


00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:42.987
Really?


00:12:43.158 --> 00:12:46.252
I always thought football players
liked to, well...


00:12:46.428 --> 00:12:48.419
- ...play the field.
- Pfft.


00:12:48.596 --> 00:12:53.659
Me too. I never thought Fred would
be the relationship type, but he totally is.


00:12:53.868 --> 00:12:55.529
I'm just not the relationship type.


00:12:55.704 --> 00:12:58.969
I'm a football player,
we like to, uh, play the field.


00:12:59.140 --> 00:13:00.971
Anyhow, it's summer, Shaggy.


00:13:01.142 --> 00:13:04.009
Oh, yeah, summer. Totally.


00:13:04.779 --> 00:13:08.943
Because who'd want a girlfriend
during daylight-savings time?


00:13:10.018 --> 00:13:11.679
Good guess, but what I'm saying...


00:13:11.853 --> 00:13:15.016
...is summer's a time you just wanna
have fun. Not get so serious.


00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.522
Daphne's cool,
she feels the same way.


00:13:17.692 --> 00:13:19.887
It's totally getting serious.


00:13:20.095 --> 00:13:22.290
Fred's cool, he feels the same way.


00:13:22.464 --> 00:13:26.662
Well, it certainly sounds
like you two are perfectly in sync.


00:13:26.835 --> 00:13:27.893
Yeah.


00:13:28.103 --> 00:13:30.094
- Exactly.
- Exactly.


00:13:30.305 --> 00:13:32.364
[SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]


00:13:33.675 --> 00:13:35.734
[YAWNS]


00:13:37.979 --> 00:13:39.207
SHAGGY:
Hey, Scoob.


00:13:39.414 --> 00:13:44.374
- How was the first dog day of summer?
- Relaxing.


00:13:44.619 --> 00:13:47.349
Glad to hear it, boy.
Now, come on, let's go get some--


00:13:47.522 --> 00:13:50.719
Oh, hello, Velma.


00:13:50.925 --> 00:13:54.088
- How was your day?
- Fine, I guess.


00:13:54.262 --> 00:13:57.561
Oh, really? Like, mine was fine too.


00:13:57.732 --> 00:14:00.257
It's crazy
how much we have in common, huh?


00:14:00.835 --> 00:14:01.927
Oh, boy.


00:14:02.137 --> 00:14:05.265
So, guys, my uncle invited us
to the opening night reception.


00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.601
- What do you say?
- Awesome.


00:14:07.776 --> 00:14:10.176
- How about a dip in the pool first?
DAPHNE: Sounds great.


00:14:12.514 --> 00:14:16.382
Oh, like, that sounds like a real rager.
What do you think, V?


00:14:16.584 --> 00:14:19.417
Perhaps I'll rendezvous
with everyone later.


00:14:19.654 --> 00:14:24.148
Since we arrived, I've been eager
to survey the indigenous flora and fauna.


00:14:24.926 --> 00:14:26.951
Oh, hey. Wait up.


00:14:27.162 --> 00:14:30.791
So you say there's both flora and fauna
out there, huh?


00:14:30.965 --> 00:14:34.901
When was the last time you heard
those two things in the same sentence?


00:14:36.304 --> 00:14:37.362
[BELCHES]


00:14:38.373 --> 00:14:42.434
Shaggy, did you know
Lake Erie is the warmest...


00:14:42.677 --> 00:14:46.044
...and most biologically productive
of the Great Lakes?


00:14:46.214 --> 00:14:49.809
Not to mention
the eleventh largest lake in the world.


00:14:49.984 --> 00:14:51.042
[METAL DETECTOR BEEPING]


00:14:51.219 --> 00:14:52.584
SHAGGY:
Oh, wow.


00:14:53.121 --> 00:14:56.557
I could listen to you talk like that
for hours.


00:14:57.625 --> 00:15:00.253
Are you really interested
in this stuff, Shaggy?


00:15:01.229 --> 00:15:06.292
I've never known you to be,
well, intellectually curious.


00:15:07.936 --> 00:15:10.427
Oh, I'm curious
about a lot of things, Velma.


00:15:10.638 --> 00:15:11.935
Like....


00:15:12.106 --> 00:15:14.666
Like people and relationships...


00:15:14.843 --> 00:15:18.335
...and relationships between people.


00:15:23.017 --> 00:15:24.917
Hey.


00:15:26.454 --> 00:15:28.115
[GRUNTING]


00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:32.787
Hey, Shaggy,
you're gonna love this factoid.


00:15:33.328 --> 00:15:37.162
Lake Erie has been gradually rising
over the last few hundred years.


00:15:37.365 --> 00:15:41.426
That means beneath
all of these rock formations...


00:15:41.603 --> 00:15:44.003
...there are miles
of underwater caves.


00:15:44.239 --> 00:15:46.833
- Get out of town.
- No, really.


00:15:47.008 --> 00:15:49.806
You can tell
by the variegated sedimentary striations.


00:15:50.445 --> 00:15:52.675
Oh, would you look at that.


00:15:52.847 --> 00:15:57.841
I've never seen irrigated rudimentary
claymations like that before.


00:15:58.953 --> 00:16:04.118
Hey, Velma, yesterday at the van....


00:16:04.459 --> 00:16:05.687
Uh....


00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:07.350
Jinkies.


00:16:07.896 --> 00:16:10.694
Look at this, Shaggy.


00:16:10.899 --> 00:16:13.891
I think it might actually
be a moonstone.


00:16:14.068 --> 00:16:15.797
They're very rare.


00:16:16.004 --> 00:16:17.995
You know,
the Native Americans believed...


00:16:18.172 --> 00:16:22.802
...they held this mystical connection
with the moon, thereby the name.


00:16:24.779 --> 00:16:27.179
Look at how it glows.


00:16:27.982 --> 00:16:30.576
It's beautiful, isn't it?


00:16:32.287 --> 00:16:34.221
It sure is.


00:16:34.389 --> 00:16:37.017
Almost as beautiful as your eyes.


00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:41.927
- Oh, Shaggy.
- Oh, Velma.


00:16:42.096 --> 00:16:45.224
Oh, Shaggy, I think I'm gonna be sick.


00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:49.803
- What? Oh, Velma, are you all right?
- I'm fine.


00:16:50.204 --> 00:16:52.502
I just feel really nauseous
all of a sudden.


00:16:52.707 --> 00:16:54.504
SHAGGY:
Like, you better sit down.


00:16:54.709 --> 00:16:56.700
- Here, let me help.
- No, it's okay.


00:16:57.078 --> 00:17:00.912
I'm just gonna go back to the room
and lie down for a little while.


00:17:02.216 --> 00:17:04.377
Oh, okay.


00:17:12.193 --> 00:17:14.525
I think she likes me.


00:17:14.762 --> 00:17:16.889
Oy vay.


00:17:19.834 --> 00:17:21.893
[PIANO PLAYING]


00:17:22.103 --> 00:17:25.095
THORNY: Well, I'll catch you out there
on the links, huh?


00:17:25.273 --> 00:17:26.535
Oh.


00:17:26.708 --> 00:17:30.109
Senator. I'm so glad
you could make it.


00:17:30.278 --> 00:17:35.375
Oh, how could I ever say no
to my biggest contributor?


00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:37.074
- How about a photograph?
- Yes.


00:17:41.089 --> 00:17:44.581
- Good thing I dressed up, hey, Scoob?
SCOOBY: Yeah.


00:17:44.759 --> 00:17:47.751
Hey, Shagg, Scoob. Where's Velma?


00:17:47.929 --> 00:17:49.328
Oh. Uh, heh.


00:17:49.497 --> 00:17:53.763
Uh, she got sick all of a sudden.
But it was totally natural causes...


00:17:53.935 --> 00:17:56.165
...and not revulsion
at the very thought of me.


00:17:57.138 --> 00:17:58.264
Okay.


00:18:01.909 --> 00:18:05.811
- Hey, Scoob, check out the buffet.
- Ooh.


00:18:06.781 --> 00:18:10.239
Now, if you don't mind,
one from my best side.


00:18:11.486 --> 00:18:12.748
One more.


00:18:17.625 --> 00:18:20.253
This will be good in my scrapbook.


00:18:21.396 --> 00:18:23.125
Perfect.


00:18:39.213 --> 00:18:41.681
Like, who ordered the pea soup?


00:18:50.358 --> 00:18:52.155
THORNY:
Sorry, everyone.


00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:55.796
I'm sure it's just a little minor glitch
with one of our generators.


00:18:55.963 --> 00:18:57.191
I'll just--


00:18:57.932 --> 00:18:58.956
[GROWLING]


00:18:59.133 --> 00:19:00.828
What the heck is that?


00:19:01.035 --> 00:19:03.128
[GASPING]


00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:08.500
- Fred?
- I don't know either, Daph.


00:19:14.348 --> 00:19:15.508
[WOMAN SCREAMS]


00:19:15.683 --> 00:19:17.173
[ROARING]


00:19:17.351 --> 00:19:20.650
SCOOBY:
Lake monster.


00:19:22.457 --> 00:19:25.858
Excuse me, I don't recall
having seen your name on the guest list.


00:19:37.071 --> 00:19:39.062
[SCREAMING]


00:19:44.912 --> 00:19:46.277
[PHOTOGRAPHER SCREAMS]


00:19:50.017 --> 00:19:52.247
That thing can't be real, can it?


00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:56.117
I don't know, but I'm not
getting close enough to find out.


00:19:57.191 --> 00:19:58.249
Hi.


00:20:00.995 --> 00:20:02.758
[ROARS]


00:20:09.504 --> 00:20:10.528
THORNY:
No, please.


00:20:10.705 --> 00:20:11.729
Please, everyone...


00:20:11.906 --> 00:20:15.034
...I'm sure there's a logical explanation
as to what's going on.


00:20:15.209 --> 00:20:16.642
We'll just tidy up the tent...


00:20:16.811 --> 00:20:20.076
...and, you know,
we'll just continue the party.


00:20:20.248 --> 00:20:21.772
Everyone-- Oh, senator, senator.


00:20:21.949 --> 00:20:25.214
MAN: Give me the keys, I'll get it myself.
WOMAN: Just go without him.


00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:27.017
My goodness.


00:20:27.755 --> 00:20:31.452
Why do I have the feeling
I missed something rather significant?


00:20:31.626 --> 00:20:35.027
It was the lake monster.
The lake monster of Erie Pointe.


00:20:35.229 --> 00:20:39.632
It was horrifying, terrifying,
scariest thing I've ever seen in my life.


00:20:39.801 --> 00:20:43.134
On a more personal note,
how are you feeling, Velma?


00:20:43.304 --> 00:20:46.762
- Did you just say the lake monster?
- Yeah.


00:20:46.941 --> 00:20:47.999
You can't be serious.


00:20:48.176 --> 00:20:51.270
Oh, my guests sure seemed to think
it was serious.


00:20:51.445 --> 00:20:53.072
Look at this, not even day one...


00:20:53.247 --> 00:20:55.738
...and half of them
have canceled their memberships.


00:20:55.917 --> 00:20:58.977
If somebody doesn't figure out
what's going on here quickly...


00:20:59.153 --> 00:21:01.951
...it's gonna be a very short summer
for all of us.


00:21:03.057 --> 00:21:05.855
Guys, we have to do something.


00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:09.188
We can't afford to lose these jobs.


00:21:17.772 --> 00:21:18.796
Oh, no.


00:21:18.973 --> 00:21:20.304
No, no, no.


00:21:20.474 --> 00:21:22.499
- You guys thinking what I'm thinking?
- No.


00:21:22.677 --> 00:21:24.611
- Come on.
- Guys, please, don't--


00:21:24.979 --> 00:21:26.003
[SIGHS]


00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:28.080
Here we go again.


00:21:28.282 --> 00:21:30.079
Uncle Thorny.


00:21:31.485 --> 00:21:34.113
We just wanna let you know
not to worry.


00:21:34.288 --> 00:21:36.017
Not only did you hire summer help...


00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:40.388
...you also hired the best supernatural
detectives in the tristate area.


00:21:40.628 --> 00:21:42.687
- I did?
- That's right.


00:21:42.864 --> 00:21:45.059
And I know just where to start too.


00:21:45.233 --> 00:21:47.531
With Elmer Uggins,
the person who's taken...


00:21:47.702 --> 00:21:50.364
...the only known photo
of the lake monster.


00:22:05.686 --> 00:22:08.154
FRED:
Heh. Would you look at that.


00:22:08.322 --> 00:22:12.224
Our first suspect just happens to be
the keeper of a creepy old lighthouse.


00:22:12.426 --> 00:22:14.053
You know, just once...


00:22:14.228 --> 00:22:19.029
...I wish we found a mystery
that started in a cheery futon showroom.


00:22:19.734 --> 00:22:20.996
What?


00:22:21.168 --> 00:22:25.332
Futons offer far more support
than traditional mattresses.


00:22:31.512 --> 00:22:33.571
[FOGHORN BLOWS]


00:22:46.460 --> 00:22:49.554
Well, looks like the light's on
but nobody's home.


00:22:49.730 --> 00:22:52.927
Isn't this the part when we normally
split up and search for clues?


00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:55.091
I'll go with Velma. Ha.


00:22:56.704 --> 00:22:58.604
Come on. It'll be fun.


00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:02.703
Okay. Come on, Daph.


00:23:09.784 --> 00:23:11.445
[SHAGGY SNIFFING]


00:23:11.619 --> 00:23:16.454
Oh, Velma, what is that sweet fragrance
you're wearing?


00:23:16.924 --> 00:23:18.619
Bug and tick repellent.


00:23:18.793 --> 00:23:19.987
[MOSQUITO BUZZING]


00:23:20.194 --> 00:23:23.595
Well, it certainly isn't repelling me.


00:23:28.803 --> 00:23:30.270
[CLEARS THROAT]


00:23:31.772 --> 00:23:34.570
It sure is a lovely night, huh?


00:23:34.742 --> 00:23:37.677
I've always enjoyed
strolling beneath a full moon.


00:23:37.845 --> 00:23:40.973
Werewolves notwithstanding,
of course.


00:23:41.415 --> 00:23:45.442
I too enjoy walking
by the light of the silvery moon.


00:23:45.619 --> 00:23:46.745
[CHUCKLES]


00:23:46.921 --> 00:23:50.322
Heh, heh, heh.
Yeah, that's a good one.


00:23:50.491 --> 00:23:52.152
Wait, where's the funny?


00:23:52.827 --> 00:23:55.523
- Oh. "By the Light of the Silvery Moon"?
- Yeah.


00:23:55.730 --> 00:23:58.528
It's just an old vaudevillian ditty.


00:23:58.766 --> 00:24:02.497
But I must confess,
I do have a soft spot for it.


00:24:04.972 --> 00:24:09.341
Like, wait, I think I do know that one.


00:24:16.650 --> 00:24:19.278
- [SINGING] By the light
CHORUS: Not the dark, but the light


00:24:19.453 --> 00:24:22.718
- Of the silvery moon
CHORUS: Not the sun, but the moon


00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:26.121
- I wanna spoon
CHORUS: Not broom, but spoon


00:24:26.293 --> 00:24:30.855
To my honey I'll croon love's tune


00:24:31.032 --> 00:24:33.899
- Honeymoon
- Honeymoon, honeymoon


00:24:34.068 --> 00:24:37.003
- Keep a-shining in June
- Keep a-shining in June


00:24:37.171 --> 00:24:40.732
Your silvery beams
Will bring love's dreams


00:24:40.908 --> 00:24:43.809
We'll be cuddling soon


00:24:44.278 --> 00:24:48.009
By the light of the silvery


00:24:48.315 --> 00:24:52.479
CHORUS: Moon
SHAGGY: Moon


00:24:52.720 --> 00:24:54.813
[RECORD SCRATCHING]


00:24:55.056 --> 00:24:57.354
ALL [SINGING]:
Act one, scene new


00:24:57.525 --> 00:25:00.016
Act two
Me, you


00:25:00.194 --> 00:25:02.185
Let's go
New tune


00:25:02.363 --> 00:25:04.160
- By the light
- Not the dark, but the light


00:25:04.331 --> 00:25:06.925
- Of the silvery moon
- Not the sun, but the moon


00:25:07.101 --> 00:25:09.262
- I wanna spoon
- Not broom, but spoon


00:25:09.437 --> 00:25:12.235
- To my honey I'll croon
- Croon! Five, six


00:25:12.406 --> 00:25:14.431
- By the moon
- By the moon, by the moon


00:25:14.608 --> 00:25:16.872
- Keep it shining in June
- Keep it shining in June


00:25:17.044 --> 00:25:19.376
Your silvery beams
Will bring love's dreams


00:25:19.547 --> 00:25:22.015
- We'll be cuddling soon
- We'll be cuddling soon


00:25:22.183 --> 00:25:25.016
By the silvery moon


00:25:37.932 --> 00:25:42.301
Hey, Fred, you don't think Shaggy
could have a crush on Velma, do you?


00:25:42.470 --> 00:25:45.735
Not unless she turned into
a steaming bowl of chili cheese fries.


00:25:45.906 --> 00:25:47.373
[CHUCKLES]


00:25:48.576 --> 00:25:50.908
- Why?
- I don't know, it's just...


00:25:51.078 --> 00:25:53.376
...he's been acting really goofy lately.


00:25:53.547 --> 00:25:55.208
Even for Shaggy.


00:25:55.382 --> 00:25:58.476
And he's been following Velma around
like a puppy dog.


00:25:58.652 --> 00:26:01.280
Actually, that would explain
why he's been asking me...


00:26:01.455 --> 00:26:03.446
...all those questions about dating.


00:26:03.624 --> 00:26:06.320
But I guess he didn't take my advice.


00:26:06.494 --> 00:26:09.088
Advice? Wait, Fred, what advice?


00:26:14.001 --> 00:26:15.468
[CREATURE GROWLING]


00:26:16.370 --> 00:26:21.398
Um, Velma, that wasn't what I thought
it was, was it?


00:26:21.575 --> 00:26:22.837
I don't know.


00:26:23.010 --> 00:26:27.777
Did you surmise that it was a heretofore
unclassified amphibious humanoid?


00:26:28.282 --> 00:26:33.185
No. I thought it was a lake monster!
Zoinks!


00:26:33.387 --> 00:26:34.786
Fred?


00:26:34.955 --> 00:26:38.584
Exactly what advice
did you give Shaggy about dating?


00:26:38.759 --> 00:26:39.783
What?


00:26:39.960 --> 00:26:44.158
Oh, you know, just that it's summertime
and we're not really--


00:26:44.331 --> 00:26:45.423
[CREATURE ROARS]


00:26:45.599 --> 00:26:46.691
Come on.


00:26:46.934 --> 00:26:48.834
Go, go, go!


00:26:49.036 --> 00:26:51.834
SHAGGY:
It's the lake monster! Save me.


00:26:52.039 --> 00:26:54.337
MONSTER:
Ow! My ankle.


00:26:54.508 --> 00:26:56.100
What?


00:27:00.281 --> 00:27:01.339
UGGINS:
Hey.


00:27:01.949 --> 00:27:03.541
Mr. Uggins, I presume?


00:27:07.521 --> 00:27:09.148
Call me Elmer.


00:27:10.958 --> 00:27:12.289
Hi, kids.


00:27:14.828 --> 00:27:18.525
So you've never actually seen
the monster?


00:27:18.699 --> 00:27:21.896
I was just using the legend
to make a quick buck.


00:27:22.069 --> 00:27:24.333
Made some postcards...


00:27:24.538 --> 00:27:27.166
...sold them to the local tourist traps.


00:27:27.942 --> 00:27:29.136
- Mm?
- No.


00:27:29.310 --> 00:27:31.175
- No.
- Thanks.


00:27:31.879 --> 00:27:32.903
Hey, what can I say?


00:27:33.080 --> 00:27:35.844
You know, lighthouse keeping
ain't exactly a growth industry.


00:27:36.016 --> 00:27:37.540
[CHUCKLING]


00:27:38.219 --> 00:27:39.743
Ahem. Anyway...


00:27:39.954 --> 00:27:43.549
...when I heard about all the hoopla
down at the country club tonight...


00:27:43.724 --> 00:27:48.218
...I figured it might be a good time
to dust off old green-eyes over there...


00:27:48.462 --> 00:27:49.986
...and take some new shots.


00:27:50.164 --> 00:27:51.722
[IMITATING CAMERA SHUTTER
CLICKING]


00:27:51.899 --> 00:27:53.230
But listen, kids...


00:27:53.467 --> 00:27:56.994
...if this thing's really back,
you best leave now while you still can.


00:27:57.204 --> 00:28:00.196
Come on, you don't really believe
the monster's real, do you?


00:28:00.407 --> 00:28:02.875
It's probably some prankster
with a better costume.


00:28:03.043 --> 00:28:05.170
Maybe it is and maybe it ain't.


00:28:05.346 --> 00:28:07.405
But one thing's for sure...


00:28:07.581 --> 00:28:11.381
...the legend is a truly terrible tale.


00:28:11.552 --> 00:28:16.012
It all goes back
to the very beginnings of town.


00:28:16.223 --> 00:28:19.351
When the first settlers arrived
in these parts...


00:28:19.526 --> 00:28:22.290
...they was confronted
by an old woman...


00:28:22.496 --> 00:28:25.693
...who was said to live
in a cave by the lake.


00:28:25.899 --> 00:28:27.696
Grubwort was her name.


00:28:27.901 --> 00:28:29.869
Wanda Grubwort.


00:28:30.037 --> 00:28:32.870
She claimed all the land around the lake
belonged to her...


00:28:33.040 --> 00:28:36.100
...and told the settlers that
if they didn't turn back...


00:28:36.644 --> 00:28:38.771
...they would pay the price.


00:28:39.380 --> 00:28:42.872
But them early pioneers was not about
to be turned away so easily...


00:28:43.050 --> 00:28:48.955
...so they settled in
and forgot all about her warning.


00:28:49.323 --> 00:28:52.884
But Wanda Grubwort did not forget.


00:28:53.060 --> 00:28:58.327
And one day,
she fulfilled her dark oath.


00:28:59.833 --> 00:29:02.631
Using her magical staff...


00:29:02.836 --> 00:29:06.795
...she cast a spell
upon an innocent creature of the lake...


00:29:07.675 --> 00:29:11.907
...transforming it into a hideous beast.


00:29:16.684 --> 00:29:19.414
Once Grubwort
had her monstrous slave...


00:29:19.586 --> 00:29:22.350
...she loosed it upon the villagers.


00:29:29.296 --> 00:29:32.288
And then? What happened next?


00:29:32.466 --> 00:29:36.459
Well, it's said the settlers
eventually overcame Grubwort...


00:29:36.637 --> 00:29:41.370
...tried her for witchery
and burned her at the stake.


00:29:44.178 --> 00:29:45.839
Like I said...


00:29:47.281 --> 00:29:50.444
...you best leave now
while you still can.


00:29:51.985 --> 00:29:54.818
I'm sorry, Mr. Uggins,
but we just don't give up that easy.


00:29:55.656 --> 00:29:59.524
He obviously wasn't
in my sophomore geometry class.


00:30:01.095 --> 00:30:02.528
[UGGINS GRUNTS]


00:30:03.464 --> 00:30:07.696
SHAGGY:
Mr. Shaggy...


00:30:08.836 --> 00:30:10.895
...Dinkley.


00:30:11.138 --> 00:30:13.606
It's like the angels are singing it.


00:30:14.141 --> 00:30:16.632
- Mister--
- Hey, Shagg. What you doing?


00:30:17.745 --> 00:30:20.236
Oh! Um-- Nothing.


00:30:27.321 --> 00:30:31.917
Doctor says I need more linen
in my diet.


00:30:32.993 --> 00:30:34.927
Okay. So, have you seen Fred?


00:30:36.063 --> 00:30:37.860
He's out on the--


00:30:38.065 --> 00:30:40.499
Out on the green,
putting with some girls.


00:30:41.335 --> 00:30:42.359
Girls?


00:30:42.536 --> 00:30:45.232
FRED:
Now, just remember to follow through.


00:30:45.739 --> 00:30:47.832
GIRL 1:
Follow through.


00:30:49.943 --> 00:30:51.774
Hey.


00:30:52.012 --> 00:30:54.173
GIRL 1: Thanks.
FRED: Okay, guys, I'm out of here.


00:30:54.915 --> 00:30:57.110
- Okay, I'll see you guys later.
- Bye.


00:30:57.284 --> 00:30:59.752
GIRL 2: Bye, Fred.
FRED: Bye now.


00:31:01.221 --> 00:31:02.586
Hey, Daph.


00:31:02.790 --> 00:31:04.451
- What's up, Shags?
- Hey, Fred.


00:31:07.961 --> 00:31:09.189
What?


00:31:09.363 --> 00:31:11.160
Hey, um...


00:31:11.932 --> 00:31:14.025
...can I ask your advice
about something?


00:31:14.201 --> 00:31:15.600
Sure.


00:31:15.803 --> 00:31:17.930
Well, I....


00:31:19.206 --> 00:31:21.197
See, I have this friend, okay?


00:31:21.375 --> 00:31:24.742
His name's, um, Scruffy. Yeah, Scruffy.
They call him that...


00:31:24.912 --> 00:31:28.109
...because he has a goatee.
No, that would be too obvious.


00:31:28.315 --> 00:31:33.719
Anyway, so this friend of mine,
who doesn't have a goatee or a dog...


00:31:33.921 --> 00:31:35.946
...definitely doesn't have
a dog either...


00:31:36.190 --> 00:31:39.682
...he has this crush on this girl
he sometimes solves mysteries with.


00:31:39.893 --> 00:31:41.986
No, no. That's a dead giveaway.


00:31:42.596 --> 00:31:44.826
- Let me start over. So--
- Shaggy.


00:31:45.566 --> 00:31:48.399
It's okay. We know you like Velma.


00:31:49.336 --> 00:31:50.394
[SCOFFS]


00:31:50.571 --> 00:31:51.833
Oh. Oh, what?


00:31:52.005 --> 00:31:54.337
Oh, I don't know
what you guys are talking about.


00:31:54.508 --> 00:31:56.908
I definitely do not like-- Velma.


00:31:57.077 --> 00:32:00.513
You are not gonna believe what I found
in the security footage. Come on.


00:32:03.750 --> 00:32:08.119
After you watch this,
I think you'll all be saying "jinkies."


00:32:09.456 --> 00:32:12.323
Hey, the security camera
caught the attack.


00:32:12.526 --> 00:32:15.825
Yep. And they caught
something else too.


00:32:19.833 --> 00:32:22.996
Looks like we have two pranksters
on our hands.


00:32:23.237 --> 00:32:24.636
Jinkies.


00:32:25.639 --> 00:32:27.937
- Told you.
- Freeze it.


00:32:28.108 --> 00:32:31.100
If you zoom in right here,
we can see who's inside that cloak.


00:32:36.850 --> 00:32:39.182
SHAGGY:
Oh, look, it's coming into focus.


00:32:40.053 --> 00:32:41.748
[SHAGGY SCREAMS]


00:32:42.656 --> 00:32:44.146
What happened?


00:32:44.324 --> 00:32:47.191
Like, that spooky figure
must be using some sort of magic...


00:32:47.361 --> 00:32:49.522
...to prevent us from seeing its face.


00:32:49.696 --> 00:32:55.066
I'm afraid the explanation is slightly
less supernatural than that, Shaggy.


00:32:55.302 --> 00:33:00.171
I accidentally knocked over my green tea
and short-circuited the hard drive.


00:33:00.674 --> 00:33:02.471
- Oh.
- That's okay, Velma.


00:33:02.676 --> 00:33:06.009
You know, I'm sure we'll find
another piece of critical evidence.


00:33:06.179 --> 00:33:07.646
- Right, guys?
- Yeah, for sure.


00:33:07.814 --> 00:33:09.145
- It's groovy.
FRED: Don't worry.


00:33:09.349 --> 00:33:12.284
I know this is highly
uncharacteristic behavior.


00:33:13.720 --> 00:33:16.086
I'm really sorry, guys.


00:33:20.928 --> 00:33:23.556
I'll tender my resignation from the group
if you wish.


00:33:23.730 --> 00:33:24.754
- What?
- What?


00:33:24.932 --> 00:33:25.990
DAPHNE: Velma.
- Come on.


00:33:26.166 --> 00:33:27.793
Velma.


00:33:30.437 --> 00:33:31.870
Like, hold on, V.


00:33:35.375 --> 00:33:39.744
Don't beat yourself up about this.
You just pulled a Shaggy, that's all.


00:33:40.514 --> 00:33:42.209
I do it all the time.


00:33:43.383 --> 00:33:46.682
Thanks, Shaggy,
but there's really no excuse.


00:33:47.688 --> 00:33:51.818
Maybe reading a little Sylvia Plath
will buoy my spirits.


00:33:52.759 --> 00:33:54.192
Hey, I....


00:33:54.361 --> 00:33:56.625
I still think you're wonderful.


00:33:56.830 --> 00:33:59.890
Shaggy, that was so nice.


00:34:00.100 --> 00:34:03.695
That's exactly how you should be
if you're really serious about Velma.


00:34:04.071 --> 00:34:06.096
Oh. Oh, what?


00:34:06.273 --> 00:34:08.207
Oh, what do you mean?


00:34:08.375 --> 00:34:09.865
I do not--


00:34:11.211 --> 00:34:12.872
All right, I admit it.


00:34:13.046 --> 00:34:14.445
I like Velma.


00:34:14.615 --> 00:34:17.846
I'm my friend. I'm Scruffy.


00:34:19.419 --> 00:34:21.284
But what am I gonna do?


00:34:21.455 --> 00:34:24.083
You know, I don't know
what I'm supposed to say to her.


00:34:24.257 --> 00:34:26.225
Let me help you out, Shags.


00:34:26.426 --> 00:34:28.121
You gotta be confident, smooth.


00:34:28.362 --> 00:34:30.227
- Girls like guys--
- Don't listen to him.


00:34:30.397 --> 00:34:32.456
He has no idea what girls like.


00:34:32.633 --> 00:34:35.227
See, what girls like is to feel special.


00:34:35.402 --> 00:34:37.768
To feel like they're the only one
on a guy's mind.


00:34:37.938 --> 00:34:40.304
Yeah, I know that.
But listen, what you wanna do--


00:34:40.474 --> 00:34:43.375
Well, if you know that,
then why don't you try it sometime?


00:34:43.577 --> 00:34:45.568
What's with you?
Why are you acting weird?


00:34:45.746 --> 00:34:48.613
- How exactly am I act--?
- Like, you know what?


00:34:48.815 --> 00:34:50.749
Forget I even asked.


00:34:50.951 --> 00:34:52.976
I'll just figure this out for myself.


00:34:53.153 --> 00:34:57.112
Besides, if I ever get Velma to like me,
I want it to be real...


00:34:57.290 --> 00:34:59.815
...not some loosey-goosey thing
like you guys have.


00:35:04.297 --> 00:35:06.527
Fred, did you say something
to Shaggy...


00:35:06.700 --> 00:35:09.999
...about us having
a "loosey-goosey" relationship?


00:35:10.203 --> 00:35:12.296
What? Oh, no, no.


00:35:13.040 --> 00:35:14.871
I just told him how we're casual.


00:35:15.042 --> 00:35:18.534
You know, how it's summer
and we're just hanging out.


00:35:19.346 --> 00:35:22.713
I mean,
that is what we're doing, right?


00:35:22.916 --> 00:35:26.977
Yes, Fred.
That is exactly what we're doing.


00:35:27.154 --> 00:35:33.024
I'm just so glad
that we're on the same page.


00:35:35.796 --> 00:35:39.823
Well, she's not the president
of the drama club for nothing.


00:35:40.934 --> 00:35:42.526
I like you, Velma Dinkley.


00:35:42.736 --> 00:35:44.203
So, what do you say?


00:35:44.438 --> 00:35:47.635
- Will you go on a date with me?
- Sorry, not my type.


00:35:47.808 --> 00:35:49.469
Like, come on, Scoob.


00:35:49.676 --> 00:35:52.076
Forget Velma.


00:35:52.946 --> 00:35:55.938
Time for a midnight snack.


00:35:56.383 --> 00:35:58.578
SHAGGY: A what?
- A midnight snack.


00:35:58.752 --> 00:36:03.382
You know, a couple of sandwiches,
a rack of ribs, pepperoni?


00:36:03.557 --> 00:36:07.493
- What?
- Oh, just follow me. Whew.


00:36:08.195 --> 00:36:09.321
Just my luck.


00:36:09.496 --> 00:36:13.091
I've got a talking dog
and I can't understand a word he says.


00:36:31.551 --> 00:36:33.610
SHAGGY:
Mm, mm, mm.


00:36:33.887 --> 00:36:36.856
Sandwich, look out.


00:36:38.625 --> 00:36:40.616
[SNIFFS THEN SIGHS]


00:36:40.794 --> 00:36:42.523
Is that Eau de' Dinkley I detect?


00:36:44.564 --> 00:36:45.758
Shaggy?


00:36:45.932 --> 00:36:50.562
Shaggy? Hey, what about
my midnight snack?


00:36:50.737 --> 00:36:52.796
[GROWLS]


00:36:54.407 --> 00:36:55.704
Huh.


00:36:56.109 --> 00:36:57.872
DAPHNE:
Nice shot.


00:37:10.157 --> 00:37:11.886
Mine.


00:37:12.092 --> 00:37:13.582
[MAN GRUNTS
AND DAPHNE SHRIEKS]


00:37:26.907 --> 00:37:28.932
Velma?


00:37:31.945 --> 00:37:34.140
Where is she?


00:37:41.154 --> 00:37:42.178
[TWIG CRACKS]


00:37:42.355 --> 00:37:43.822
[SIGHS]


00:37:47.828 --> 00:37:50.353
Oh, Velma, is that you?


00:37:53.800 --> 00:37:54.824
[ROARS]


00:37:55.202 --> 00:37:56.430
[SCREAMS]


00:37:59.840 --> 00:38:00.864
Oh, hi, Fred.


00:38:02.776 --> 00:38:04.107
Is something wrong?


00:38:04.311 --> 00:38:06.040
SHAGGY:
Help!


00:38:06.213 --> 00:38:08.511
- Help, help!
- Come on.


00:38:09.583 --> 00:38:10.845
- Shaggy.
- Aah!


00:38:11.017 --> 00:38:12.678
- What's wrong?
- Oh.


00:38:12.853 --> 00:38:14.514
Oh, you know, nothing.


00:38:14.688 --> 00:38:17.179
I just thought I'd work
on my blood-curdling scream.


00:38:17.357 --> 00:38:20.190
What the heck do you think is wrong?
It's the lake monster.


00:38:20.694 --> 00:38:21.718
Whoa!


00:38:23.530 --> 00:38:26.795
That's it, time to unmask this prankster
once and for all.


00:38:27.000 --> 00:38:29.093
[GRUNTING]


00:38:29.903 --> 00:38:32.531
Come on, help me with this mask.


00:38:36.109 --> 00:38:38.475
Fred, I don't think this thing
is a mask.


00:38:42.215 --> 00:38:45.116
Ew! Gross.


00:38:45.652 --> 00:38:47.620
FRED:
Keep moving.


00:38:49.923 --> 00:38:52.084
This thing keeps getting
the jump on us.


00:38:52.259 --> 00:38:55.353
It can't jump in two directions.
Come on, split up.


00:39:00.734 --> 00:39:02.361
Like, why did he have to pick me?


00:39:02.535 --> 00:39:05.504
In gym class,
I'm always the last one picked.


00:39:06.206 --> 00:39:07.230
Huh. Heh.


00:39:07.407 --> 00:39:09.068
Oh, zoinks.


00:39:09.242 --> 00:39:11.437
[ROARING]


00:39:15.548 --> 00:39:17.539
SCOOBY:
I'll save you, Shaggy.


00:39:21.187 --> 00:39:22.245
SHAGGY:
Like, thanks, buddy.


00:39:22.422 --> 00:39:25.152
I thought that giant mutant frog
was gonna make me croak.


00:39:25.358 --> 00:39:26.382
[SHAGGY GIGGLES]


00:39:26.559 --> 00:39:29.528
Oh, boy, I wish I could enjoy that one.


00:39:31.464 --> 00:39:34.024
Oh, heh. Oh. You did it, boy.


00:39:34.601 --> 00:39:35.863
Oh, what a friend.


00:39:36.036 --> 00:39:37.435
What a pal.


00:39:37.604 --> 00:39:38.696
What a sand trap.


00:39:39.105 --> 00:39:41.198
[BOTH SCREAMING]


00:39:47.447 --> 00:39:50.939
Oh, boy, Scoob.
I owe you one, buddy.


00:39:51.117 --> 00:39:53.745
If it wasn't for you, I would--


00:39:53.954 --> 00:39:56.616
Hey, would you look at that?


00:39:59.626 --> 00:40:01.821
- It's one of those moonstones.
- Yeah.


00:40:01.995 --> 00:40:05.590
Velma loves these things almost
as much I love deep-fried--


00:40:05.765 --> 00:40:07.562
Well, anything. Huh.


00:40:07.767 --> 00:40:09.496
Groovy.


00:40:09.803 --> 00:40:11.566
Huh? Hmph.


00:40:11.738 --> 00:40:14.639
Velma, Velma, Velma. Pfft.


00:40:17.711 --> 00:40:20.475
Hey, come on,
I think the coast is clear.


00:40:21.348 --> 00:40:24.476
This doesn't make sense.
There's no such thing as a lake monster.


00:40:24.651 --> 00:40:28.246
Tell that to the thing
that just threw up an aquarium.


00:40:28.521 --> 00:40:31.490
So now do you wanna tell me
who those guys were?


00:40:31.658 --> 00:40:33.023
Not now, Fred.


00:40:34.961 --> 00:40:37.020
[MONSTER GROWLING]


00:40:42.035 --> 00:40:44.868
Oh, that was worse than my date
with Herbie Zimmer.


00:40:45.105 --> 00:40:47.869
Totally, I-- Wait, you went on a date
with Herbie Zi--?


00:40:48.942 --> 00:40:51.001
[MONSTER SCREAMING]


00:41:03.456 --> 00:41:04.684
WOMAN:
Creature.


00:41:05.492 --> 00:41:08.655
What are you doing?
You're supposed to be searching.


00:41:08.828 --> 00:41:10.887
With all the bedlam
you've raised tonight...


00:41:11.064 --> 00:41:12.861
...we'll have to stop early.


00:41:13.033 --> 00:41:14.466
Return to the lake.


00:41:14.634 --> 00:41:18.263
I'll summon you
when it's safe to resume our search.


00:41:28.048 --> 00:41:29.345
[DAPHNE SIGHS]


00:41:29.883 --> 00:41:32.283
- That was close.
- Yeah.


00:41:34.154 --> 00:41:36.884
Hey. Not bad.


00:41:37.090 --> 00:41:38.557
[SIGHS]


00:41:39.426 --> 00:41:41.485
Uncle Thorny.


00:41:42.328 --> 00:41:43.659
That thing came back.


00:41:43.830 --> 00:41:46.094
Oh, you think?


00:41:47.934 --> 00:41:51.335
Canceled memberships
and now all this damage.


00:41:52.072 --> 00:41:55.838
I hate to say it, I may have no choice
but to shut this place down...


00:41:56.009 --> 00:41:59.570
...and go back to my life
as an international playboy.


00:42:02.615 --> 00:42:03.741
SHAGGY:
Hey, guys.


00:42:03.950 --> 00:42:05.440
Shaggy, you're okay.


00:42:05.618 --> 00:42:09.281
Well, yeah, I am,
but has anyone seen Velma?


00:42:09.456 --> 00:42:12.619
Before the monster attacked,
she was out here, I know it.


00:42:12.826 --> 00:42:13.918
Oh, no.


00:42:14.094 --> 00:42:16.756
Oh, you don't think the lake monster
got to her, do you?


00:42:16.930 --> 00:42:19.728
I've seen monster movies,
I know how this works.


00:42:19.899 --> 00:42:21.628
[ROARS THEN SCREAMS]


00:42:21.835 --> 00:42:24.804
Shaggy, Shaggy. Calm down, okay?


00:42:24.971 --> 00:42:26.302
- We're gonna find her.
- Yeah.


00:42:26.473 --> 00:42:27.531
- Let's go.
SHAGGY: Okay.


00:42:27.707 --> 00:42:30.232
FRED:
Velma!


00:42:31.978 --> 00:42:33.809
DAPHNE:
Velma!


00:42:33.980 --> 00:42:35.572
Velma?


00:42:35.748 --> 00:42:36.772
Where are you?


00:42:36.950 --> 00:42:39.851
- Velma!
- Velma!


00:42:41.721 --> 00:42:44.451
Hey, guys, I found her.


00:42:49.662 --> 00:42:52.961
- Oh, no. She's dead.
- Oh!


00:42:53.133 --> 00:42:55.727
Oh, she looks so peaceful.


00:42:55.902 --> 00:42:58.393
Oh, I can't look.


00:42:58.805 --> 00:42:59.931
[GROANS]


00:43:00.440 --> 00:43:02.874
Uh.... Guys?


00:43:05.612 --> 00:43:08.479
- What's going on?
- Oh, it's a miracle.


00:43:08.648 --> 00:43:11.276
FRED: What happened to you
last night, Velma?


00:43:11.684 --> 00:43:13.311
I don't know.


00:43:14.254 --> 00:43:17.883
I couldn't sleep,
so I went for a walk by the lake.


00:43:18.324 --> 00:43:20.519
But then that fog rolled in and....


00:43:21.794 --> 00:43:25.093
Well, I must have gotten lost.


00:43:25.265 --> 00:43:27.825
I sat down to wait until it lifted...


00:43:28.034 --> 00:43:30.298
...and I must have fallen asleep.


00:43:30.770 --> 00:43:33.170
Don't you ever do that to us again,
you hear?


00:43:33.339 --> 00:43:36.308
You had us all worried so--
What are those?


00:43:39.145 --> 00:43:42.012
- They kind of look like warts.
- Warts?


00:43:42.182 --> 00:43:43.774
Egads.


00:43:43.950 --> 00:43:45.815
Oh, no.


00:43:45.985 --> 00:43:51.821
I'm sure it's just some kind
of urushiol-induced dermatitis.


00:43:51.991 --> 00:43:53.982
- Oh.
- Yeah.


00:43:55.128 --> 00:43:58.222
Anyway, what's going on?


00:43:58.431 --> 00:44:01.628
You missed another attack.
Come on, we'll get you cleaned up...


00:44:01.801 --> 00:44:04.531
- ...and we'll fill you in.
VELMA: Another attack?


00:44:04.704 --> 00:44:07.502
Anybody else hungry? I know I am.


00:44:07.674 --> 00:44:08.800
Shocking.


00:44:09.008 --> 00:44:10.475
Mm.


00:44:11.177 --> 00:44:12.201
Ooh.


00:44:12.378 --> 00:44:15.211
So you think the monster's real
and someone's using it...


00:44:15.381 --> 00:44:16.871
...to dig up something
on the grounds?


00:44:17.050 --> 00:44:20.349
Yeah. Problem is, we don't have
a single clue about who's using it.


00:44:20.553 --> 00:44:25.684
Yes, we do. The mysterious figure
had a streak of purple paint on its cloak.


00:44:27.060 --> 00:44:29.995
- So?
- So remember the boat that we passed...


00:44:30.163 --> 00:44:33.428
...on the way up here?
Shaggy called it the S.S. Daphne.


00:44:33.600 --> 00:44:35.898
It was being painted
the exact same color.


00:44:36.102 --> 00:44:40.562
I'd be willing to bet that whoever's
behind this has been on that boat.


00:44:40.773 --> 00:44:42.866
All right, gang,
we know what we have to do.


00:44:43.343 --> 00:44:46.904
After our shifts tonight, we'll head
to the docks and we'll check it out.


00:44:49.182 --> 00:44:50.206
No.


00:44:52.885 --> 00:44:54.512
No.


00:44:54.988 --> 00:44:57.582
I'm not going
until I do what I've been trying to do...


00:44:57.757 --> 00:44:59.748
...since we first got here.


00:45:02.495 --> 00:45:07.194
Um, Velma, I learned something today.


00:45:07.367 --> 00:45:09.892
Life is like a chocolate soufflé.


00:45:10.603 --> 00:45:14.903
And if you wait too long to dig in,
it could just collapse on you.


00:45:15.575 --> 00:45:19.739
So anyway,
what I'm trying to say is...


00:45:24.284 --> 00:45:27.913
...Velma Dinkley,
will you go on a date with me?


00:45:29.022 --> 00:45:31.547
- Heh. A date?
- Yeah.


00:45:32.592 --> 00:45:34.423
Shaggy.


00:45:35.662 --> 00:45:37.323
Are you serious?


00:45:37.530 --> 00:45:41.330
I've never been more serious
about anything in my entire life.


00:45:41.567 --> 00:45:45.230
Except maybe dinosaurs,
but that was a long time ago.


00:45:46.439 --> 00:45:50.398
Shaggy, that's very sweet of you...


00:45:51.311 --> 00:45:54.838
...but we're right in the middle
of an investigation.


00:45:55.782 --> 00:45:58.808
Well, like,
I think Fred and Daphne can handle it.


00:45:59.052 --> 00:46:02.647
They probably wanna spend some
quality time together anyway, right?


00:46:02.822 --> 00:46:04.483
- No, not really.
- I'm good.


00:46:05.591 --> 00:46:07.957
I don't know, Shaggy.


00:46:08.127 --> 00:46:09.185
SHAGGY:
Oh.


00:46:10.596 --> 00:46:13.030
Like-- Like, yeah, that's--


00:46:13.199 --> 00:46:14.496
I mean, that's fine.


00:46:14.701 --> 00:46:16.066
I--


00:46:16.636 --> 00:46:19.298
If I were you, I probably
wouldn't wanna go on a date...


00:46:19.472 --> 00:46:21.770
...with a goofy guy
like me either so....


00:46:27.180 --> 00:46:29.080
Hold on.


00:46:29.782 --> 00:46:31.613
Shaggy, you know what?


00:46:32.318 --> 00:46:34.786
I will go on a date with you tonight.


00:46:35.355 --> 00:46:36.379
Oh, really?


00:46:37.824 --> 00:46:39.724
- You mean it?
- Sure.


00:46:39.892 --> 00:46:40.950
Why not?


00:46:41.160 --> 00:46:43.287
Yes.


00:46:43.830 --> 00:46:45.388
Pick you up around 7.


00:46:47.133 --> 00:46:48.600
[GRUNTS]


00:46:49.168 --> 00:46:50.226
Seven o'clock.


00:46:53.973 --> 00:46:55.463
Slippery.


00:46:56.342 --> 00:46:57.366
[PIANO CRASHES]


00:46:57.543 --> 00:46:59.135
- Ouch.
SHAGGY: I'm okay.


00:47:02.648 --> 00:47:04.809
Oh, curse this mop top.


00:47:04.984 --> 00:47:07.646
I can't do anything with it.


00:47:10.156 --> 00:47:12.590
Okay, Scoob, how do I look?


00:47:12.759 --> 00:47:14.920
Ah. Handsome as a devil.


00:47:15.128 --> 00:47:17.619
What about me?


00:47:18.030 --> 00:47:19.429
Oh. Um....


00:47:19.632 --> 00:47:21.657
Like, as dapper as a Dalmatian...


00:47:21.834 --> 00:47:26.362
- ...but where are you headed, buddy?
- With you. Where else?


00:47:26.572 --> 00:47:30.201
Oh, um, heh. Um....


00:47:30.410 --> 00:47:33.004
You know, buddy...


00:47:33.179 --> 00:47:36.910
...I'm gonna have to fly solo
on this one tonight.


00:47:37.083 --> 00:47:39.847
- Solo?
- Yeah, you know, like...


00:47:40.019 --> 00:47:43.352
...you're just gonna have to do
your own thing, you know what I mean?


00:47:43.523 --> 00:47:47.459
My own thing? But, Shaggy--


00:47:47.660 --> 00:47:50.788
Thanks for understanding, Scoob.


00:47:51.697 --> 00:47:53.028
[SIGHS]


00:47:53.199 --> 00:47:55.064
I'll see you later, pal.


00:47:55.234 --> 00:47:58.032
Goodbye, Shaggy.


00:47:58.204 --> 00:48:00.263
[CRYING]


00:48:11.184 --> 00:48:13.118
[SHAGGY WHIMPERING]


00:48:13.286 --> 00:48:16.744
Who's the best puppy
in the whole wide world?


00:48:18.291 --> 00:48:20.384
[CONTINUES WHIMPERING]


00:48:22.128 --> 00:48:26.064
No. No more rolling over.


00:48:39.512 --> 00:48:40.672
- Ready?
- Yeah.


00:48:40.847 --> 00:48:43.077
Good. So...


00:48:43.249 --> 00:48:44.841
...who were they?


00:48:45.017 --> 00:48:46.780
Who were who?


00:48:47.620 --> 00:48:48.678
Oh, ho.


00:48:48.855 --> 00:48:52.757
Are you still wondering about those boys
I was playing tennis with?


00:48:52.925 --> 00:48:55.621
They were nobody, Fred.
Just some caddies I met.


00:48:55.795 --> 00:48:57.262
Why?


00:48:57.763 --> 00:48:59.253
You're not jealous, are you?


00:48:59.432 --> 00:49:01.764
Jealous? No, no.


00:49:01.934 --> 00:49:03.765
I'm not jealous. No way.


00:49:03.936 --> 00:49:05.995
I don't get jealous.


00:49:06.172 --> 00:49:08.003
Yeah, right.


00:49:22.622 --> 00:49:24.055
[SNIFFING]


00:49:28.294 --> 00:49:30.854
- Good evening, Norville.
- Heh.


00:49:31.330 --> 00:49:32.797
[CHUCKLES]


00:49:33.466 --> 00:49:35.127
Shaggy.


00:49:36.002 --> 00:49:37.765
Aren't you gonna say anything?


00:49:41.007 --> 00:49:44.204
I like corn dogs.


00:49:51.307 --> 00:49:53.741
- Thanks, Shaggy.
- Yeah.


00:49:57.380 --> 00:49:58.938
Thank you.


00:49:59.816 --> 00:50:01.841
Oh. Ahem.


00:50:14.397 --> 00:50:15.625
[CLEARS THROAT]


00:50:17.734 --> 00:50:20.635
Well, it looks like we got
the whole place to ourselves.


00:50:20.870 --> 00:50:26.069
Yes, unfortunately, that only emphasizes
the urgency of our investigation.


00:50:26.276 --> 00:50:28.972
- Sure we shouldn't check with Fred--?
- Oh, come on, V.


00:50:29.145 --> 00:50:32.774
Like, just try to put those frontal lobes
on the back burner tonight, okay?


00:50:34.117 --> 00:50:35.880
Okay, Shaggy.


00:50:36.052 --> 00:50:39.954
I must admit, I do have a hard time
letting myself relax.


00:50:40.156 --> 00:50:42.124
Especially recently.


00:50:42.358 --> 00:50:45.987
Ever since we've been here,
I just haven't felt Iike myself.


00:50:48.498 --> 00:50:51.490
Well, whoever you are, I like it.


00:50:53.503 --> 00:50:54.731
Thanks, Shaggy.


00:50:57.006 --> 00:50:58.337
Oh. Um....


00:50:58.508 --> 00:51:02.774
Now, come on,
I want this night to be perfect.


00:51:03.613 --> 00:51:05.080
[SCREAMS]


00:51:06.182 --> 00:51:07.274
Velma.


00:51:08.618 --> 00:51:10.415
VELMA:
My glasses.


00:51:10.587 --> 00:51:11.918
Here, let me help you up.


00:51:12.088 --> 00:51:13.180
Are you okay?


00:51:13.389 --> 00:51:14.788
I'm sorry, I--


00:51:14.958 --> 00:51:17.586
I don't know what came over me.


00:51:18.294 --> 00:51:19.989
Oh, here. Here you go.


00:51:20.163 --> 00:51:21.425
- Thanks.
- Yeah.


00:51:25.168 --> 00:51:28.399
Oh, boy.
Here, let me get you some water.


00:51:28.605 --> 00:51:32.200
Garçon, water, please.


00:51:32.709 --> 00:51:34.768
[SPEAKING IN FRENCH]


00:51:34.978 --> 00:51:36.002
[LAUGHING]


00:51:36.980 --> 00:51:38.845
[HUMMING]


00:51:43.920 --> 00:51:44.944
[SCOOBY BELCHES]


00:51:45.121 --> 00:51:46.349
[SCOOBY SPEAKING IN FRENCH]


00:51:47.223 --> 00:51:50.715
Oh, whoops.
I seem to have dropped my fork.


00:51:51.494 --> 00:51:54.156
Here, help me find it, waiter.


00:51:55.365 --> 00:51:57.060
Scooby-Doo, what are you doing?


00:51:57.233 --> 00:52:00.361
Waiting tables. Fresh ground pepper?


00:52:00.536 --> 00:52:03.471
Scooby, get out of here, buddy.
You're gonna ruin everything.


00:52:03.640 --> 00:52:05.369
No.


00:52:05.875 --> 00:52:10.335
Okay, but would you do it
for a Scooby snack?


00:52:10.513 --> 00:52:13.346
I can't be bought. Hmph.


00:52:14.217 --> 00:52:15.411
Now, you listen, Scoob...


00:52:15.585 --> 00:52:18.577
...I'm the master and I command you
to go back to your room...


00:52:18.755 --> 00:52:21.849
...and quit being such a bad dog.


00:52:23.760 --> 00:52:25.193
Puppy loving....


00:52:25.395 --> 00:52:27.488
[SCOOBY MUTTERING INDISTINCTLY]


00:52:28.498 --> 00:52:30.363
Bad dog? Huh.


00:52:30.566 --> 00:52:32.864
I'll show you a bad dog.


00:52:33.169 --> 00:52:35.364
[LAUGHS THEN GROWLS]


00:52:35.772 --> 00:52:37.831
No, Shaggy, don't.
The waiter will bring--


00:52:38.007 --> 00:52:39.338
[SCREAMS]


00:52:40.677 --> 00:52:42.406
Would you care to hear our specials?


00:52:42.578 --> 00:52:44.739
Scooby-Doo? Is that you?


00:52:44.981 --> 00:52:46.778
I didn't invite him.


00:52:47.016 --> 00:52:50.179
He just showed up
and tried to sabotage everything and--


00:52:50.353 --> 00:52:52.685
- And--
- Is that what I think it is?


00:52:54.991 --> 00:52:56.219
Oh, uh, heh.


00:52:56.392 --> 00:52:59.884
Yeah, that was supposed to be
a surprise.


00:53:00.096 --> 00:53:02.257
I found it in a sand trap last night.


00:53:02.498 --> 00:53:05.228
It's one of those moonstones, right?


00:53:05.802 --> 00:53:06.860
Yes.


00:53:07.070 --> 00:53:11.063
I was gonna give it to you when I walked
you back to your room tonight, but....


00:53:11.240 --> 00:53:13.401
It's beautiful.


00:53:15.545 --> 00:53:18.139
Excuse me, I have to go now.


00:53:18.815 --> 00:53:21.909
Wait, what? Well, Velma--


00:53:24.520 --> 00:53:26.317
This is all your fault, Scooby-Doo.


00:53:26.522 --> 00:53:28.387
You ruined everything.


00:53:28.558 --> 00:53:31.152
No, I didn't.


00:53:31.327 --> 00:53:32.794
[SCOOBY GROWLS]


00:53:42.105 --> 00:53:44.733
DAPHNE:
There it is, the purple boat.


00:53:44.907 --> 00:53:47.068
FRED:
She. There she is.


00:53:47.276 --> 00:53:48.675
A boat is a she, like a girl.


00:53:48.845 --> 00:53:51.006
But not one who goes around
playing tennis...


00:53:51.180 --> 00:53:53.648
...with every boy boat in the harbor.


00:54:03.693 --> 00:54:06.093
That cloaked figure
was definitely here.


00:54:06.262 --> 00:54:08.423
All hands on deck.


00:54:30.286 --> 00:54:32.948
Fred, look.


00:54:43.699 --> 00:54:45.826
- Ladies first.
- Mm-mm.


00:54:46.002 --> 00:54:47.492
Fine.


00:55:29.946 --> 00:55:32.506
Looks like a bunch of old newspapers.


00:55:32.682 --> 00:55:33.910
DAPHNE:
I'll say.


00:55:34.183 --> 00:55:35.650
FRED:
Huh.


00:55:36.953 --> 00:55:41.890
Hey, these are about that witch
from Uggins' story, Wanda Grubwort.


00:55:42.058 --> 00:55:44.959
DAPHNE: Evil staff?
- Yeah, remember? Didn't Elmer say...


00:55:45.161 --> 00:55:48.153
...an ancient staff was the source
of her black magic?


00:55:50.299 --> 00:55:51.960
DAPHNE:
Hey, look at this one.


00:55:54.036 --> 00:55:58.302
That must be what the monster's doing,
looking for the source of her powers.


00:55:58.474 --> 00:56:01.705
The problem is we still don't know
who's controlling it.


00:56:02.678 --> 00:56:05.374
Wait a second, maybe we do.


00:56:07.416 --> 00:56:11.113
Wanda Grubwort had children. She could
still have descendants living in town.


00:56:11.287 --> 00:56:12.549
Maybe one got angry...


00:56:12.722 --> 00:56:15.885
...when your uncle built on their land
and decided to get revenge.


00:56:18.628 --> 00:56:20.425
What was that?


00:56:23.199 --> 00:56:25.497
It's locked. Hello!


00:56:25.735 --> 00:56:27.430
Help. Help.


00:56:27.603 --> 00:56:31.198
DAPHNE:
Anyone out there? Let us out.


00:56:33.609 --> 00:56:34.667
Help. Help.


00:56:34.844 --> 00:56:37.142
Is anyone out there? Oh, great.


00:56:37.313 --> 00:56:39.645
If we don't get this open,
we'll be stuck here all night.


00:56:39.815 --> 00:56:41.305
[RUMBLING]


00:56:42.418 --> 00:56:44.249
That might be the least
of our worries.


00:56:45.154 --> 00:56:46.519
- Hello!
- Is anyone out there?


00:56:46.722 --> 00:56:47.746
Help!


00:56:48.624 --> 00:56:50.922
- Help, help!
DAPHNE: We need to get out.


00:56:51.093 --> 00:56:52.788
FRED: Help, anybody.
DAPHNE: Anyone!


00:56:52.995 --> 00:56:55.793
FRED: Help, anybody!
- Help, get us out!


00:56:55.965 --> 00:56:58.263
FRED:
Help, help, anybody!


00:56:58.467 --> 00:57:01.925
- Help, help.
- We're stuck, it's filling.


00:57:02.772 --> 00:57:05.468
Fred, you need to do something.
We're gonna drown.


00:57:05.675 --> 00:57:09.634
I have an idea. Why don't we call
those guys you were playing tennis with?


00:57:09.812 --> 00:57:13.543
- I knew it, you are jealous.
- Yeah, maybe I am.


00:57:13.749 --> 00:57:17.116
- Good, that was the point.
- You were just lying to make me jealous?


00:57:17.286 --> 00:57:20.722
Yes, I'm trying to pay you back
for playing golf with those floozies.


00:57:20.890 --> 00:57:23.120
Flooz--? Oh, that was different.


00:57:23.292 --> 00:57:25.317
How? How was that any different?


00:57:25.494 --> 00:57:27.826
I don't know, they were-- It just was.


00:57:27.997 --> 00:57:29.658
All right, you know what, Fred?


00:57:29.832 --> 00:57:33.165
If I'm gonna die,
I don't want to die dating a jerk.


00:57:33.336 --> 00:57:36.999
Yeah, well, if I'm gonna die,
I don't want to die dating a sneaky...


00:57:37.673 --> 00:57:40.506
...manipulative, game-playing....


00:57:46.048 --> 00:57:48.482
You see that? I saved us.


00:57:48.651 --> 00:57:52.087
That's Iovely,
but we're still broken up.


00:57:52.288 --> 00:57:53.312
What?


00:57:53.522 --> 00:57:55.217
Good.


00:57:55.925 --> 00:57:58.018
[MUTTERING]


00:58:21.083 --> 00:58:22.880
Like, what happened to you guys?


00:58:23.085 --> 00:58:24.416
What happened?


00:58:24.587 --> 00:58:26.248
We broke up, that's what happened.


00:58:26.455 --> 00:58:28.685
Yeah, best decision I ever made too.


00:58:28.891 --> 00:58:31.382
Did you just say best decision
you ever made?


00:58:31.560 --> 00:58:34.085
That's funny,
because I broke up with you.


00:58:34.263 --> 00:58:35.287
[BOTH CHUCKLE]


00:58:35.464 --> 00:58:37.193
What? You did not.


00:58:37.366 --> 00:58:39.061
- Guys?
DAPHNE: I did so.


00:58:39.235 --> 00:58:40.896
Guys.


00:58:41.103 --> 00:58:46.439
That's a real bummer and all,
but I kind of meant, why are you wet?


00:58:46.776 --> 00:58:48.266
Oh, that.


00:58:48.444 --> 00:58:51.436
Well, let's just say we almost got in
over our heads.


00:58:51.614 --> 00:58:54.708
But we figured out
that Wanda Grubwort's descendant...


00:58:54.884 --> 00:58:58.650
...might be trying to reconstruct
her magical staff.


00:59:01.624 --> 00:59:05.219
Hey, how'd it go with Velma?


00:59:06.595 --> 00:59:09.894
Yeah. Ask my waiter.


00:59:10.099 --> 00:59:12.465
DAPHNE:
Grubek, Grubel, Guzzak.


00:59:13.269 --> 00:59:14.293
No Grubwort.


00:59:14.970 --> 00:59:19.771
Huh. Would you look at that.
What a crazy coincidence.


00:59:20.810 --> 00:59:22.869
What's that, Shags?


00:59:23.312 --> 00:59:27.408
Oh. Remember that creepy general store
we stopped at on the way in?


00:59:27.950 --> 00:59:30.077
It was called Trowburgs.


00:59:30.252 --> 00:59:34.780
Well, if you spell Trowburg backwards
you get Grubwort.


00:59:34.990 --> 00:59:36.321
What are the odds, huh?


00:59:36.492 --> 00:59:40.019
Excuse me,
you are on my side of the room.


00:59:49.839 --> 00:59:51.306
[SHAGGY & SCOOBY GULP]


01:00:04.186 --> 01:00:05.483
[THUNDER CRASHING]


01:00:07.289 --> 01:00:09.223
There. Shaggy, Scooby,
go around back.


01:00:09.425 --> 01:00:11.723
- I'm not going with him.
- I'm not going with him.


01:00:11.927 --> 01:00:14.259
- You think I want to go with you?
SHAGGY: Seriously--


01:00:14.430 --> 01:00:16.295
SCOOBY: I'm not going with Shaggy.
FRED: Enough.


01:00:16.465 --> 01:00:18.626
- Guys, let's just go.
- Go.


01:00:22.638 --> 01:00:24.367
- Surprise.
WOMAN: Oh, no.


01:00:24.540 --> 01:00:25.973
[WOMAN CACKLING]


01:00:26.142 --> 01:00:27.803
Come on.


01:00:28.511 --> 01:00:29.978
Hey, wait for me.


01:00:40.156 --> 01:00:41.851
In here.


01:00:49.899 --> 01:00:51.696
SCOOBY:
This way.


01:00:52.468 --> 01:00:54.095
The other way.


01:00:59.208 --> 01:01:00.675
[SHAGGY SCREAMING]


01:01:03.846 --> 01:01:04.870
No.


01:01:06.615 --> 01:01:09.243
FRED: Come on.
SHAGGY: No, please.


01:01:09.418 --> 01:01:10.976
Please.


01:01:17.726 --> 01:01:19.887
- Now can we split up?
- Ugh.


01:01:24.934 --> 01:01:27.528
SHAGGY: Hey, come on, Scoob.
- I'm right behind you, Shaggy.


01:01:27.703 --> 01:01:29.762
[SHAGGY SCREAMS]


01:01:30.306 --> 01:01:32.536
Change of plans.


01:01:36.011 --> 01:01:38.912
WOMAN:
And stay out.


01:01:41.717 --> 01:01:44.880
Time to unmask
the person behind this mystery.


01:01:46.589 --> 01:01:49.285
- It's you?
- What?


01:01:49.458 --> 01:01:51.653
Like, it can't be.


01:01:54.029 --> 01:01:55.257
Velma?


01:01:56.232 --> 01:01:59.565
[IN DISTORTED VOICE]
Oh, you fools. I'm not Velma.


01:02:00.603 --> 01:02:02.002
[DAPHNE SCREAMS]


01:02:02.171 --> 01:02:04.071
Daphne.


01:02:05.574 --> 01:02:07.633
I don't want to hurt you, Velma.


01:02:07.843 --> 01:02:10.539
Oh, but I do want to hurt you,
pretty boy.


01:02:12.081 --> 01:02:13.571
Sorry, Velma.


01:02:13.749 --> 01:02:15.944
[GRUNTING]


01:02:21.190 --> 01:02:24.990
Velma. What's going on?
Why are you doing this?


01:02:25.194 --> 01:02:26.957
Our date wasn't that bad, was it?


01:02:27.162 --> 01:02:32.623
Why? To make them pay,
to make them all pay.


01:02:32.801 --> 01:02:37.761
Now, that I've rebuilt my staff,
no one can stop me.


01:02:45.881 --> 01:02:47.348
[COUGHING]


01:02:55.724 --> 01:03:00.627
Well, there's another mystery solved,
huh, gang?


01:03:01.196 --> 01:03:02.493
I got it.


01:03:02.665 --> 01:03:04.326
Okay.


01:03:05.601 --> 01:03:09.799
What in the world is going on?
Why is Velma doing this?


01:03:10.306 --> 01:03:11.603
Oh, no.


01:03:11.807 --> 01:03:14.674
You don't think my passions
drove her mad, do you?


01:03:14.843 --> 01:03:17.334
I'm sure there's something bigger
than that going on.


01:03:17.513 --> 01:03:18.810
I'll say.


01:03:19.848 --> 01:03:24.547
Your friend has been possessed by
the spirit of the witch Wanda Grubwort.


01:03:25.220 --> 01:03:29.987
Oh, great, my first love
and she's turned into an evil witch.


01:03:30.159 --> 01:03:32.218
Join the club.


01:03:40.669 --> 01:03:43.194
Yeah. Hee, hee, hee.


01:03:43.372 --> 01:03:44.532
It was that staff.


01:03:44.707 --> 01:03:46.072
[IMITATES EXPLOSION]


01:03:46.241 --> 01:03:48.607
She must have found the pieces...


01:03:48.777 --> 01:03:52.577
...that have been buried
all these many years.


01:03:53.215 --> 01:03:55.740
Like, by any chance...


01:03:55.918 --> 01:03:58.682
...did moonstones
play any part in this?


01:03:59.254 --> 01:04:02.917
As soon as your friend touched one
of those rocks...


01:04:03.092 --> 01:04:06.459
...the spirit of my evil ancestor
took hold of her...


01:04:06.662 --> 01:04:10.063
...and compelled her to find the rest.


01:04:10.232 --> 01:04:12.792
SCOOBY: For you, old lady.
- Oh.


01:04:14.069 --> 01:04:17.527
So it's been Velma the entire time?


01:04:17.740 --> 01:04:21.540
Like, zoinks.
It's been right under our noses.


01:04:21.744 --> 01:04:24.235
The evil spirit must have first taken
hold of her...


01:04:24.413 --> 01:04:26.472
...when we found that stone
by the lake.


01:04:27.282 --> 01:04:31.480
And those creepy warts, it was like
she was actually turning into a witch.


01:04:31.720 --> 01:04:33.119
Being burned at the stake...


01:04:33.288 --> 01:04:36.223
...would make me pretty freaked out
at the sight of fire too.


01:04:36.425 --> 01:04:39.417
And I bet she intentionally shorted out
the security console...


01:04:39.595 --> 01:04:41.995
...because she knew
we'd see her face.


01:04:42.598 --> 01:04:44.623
I can't believe we missed it.


01:04:44.800 --> 01:04:47.792
I guess we were all too wrapped up
in our own little dramas...


01:04:47.970 --> 01:04:50.438
...to catch the really big one going on.


01:04:51.273 --> 01:04:52.297
[SIGHS]


01:04:52.808 --> 01:04:58.246
So now that she has her powers back,
what's Wanda Grubwort going to do?


01:04:58.414 --> 01:05:01.850
I fear that what she seeks
is the revenge...


01:05:02.017 --> 01:05:05.453
...that has eluded her all these years.


01:05:06.221 --> 01:05:08.018
Who cares about what she wants.


01:05:08.223 --> 01:05:12.250
We gotta save Velma. Do you have
any idea where she would have gone?


01:05:12.461 --> 01:05:15.157
Oh, probably to the caves
where she lived.


01:05:15.330 --> 01:05:16.592
The caves?


01:05:16.799 --> 01:05:19.495
But what about the irrigated
rudimentary claymations?


01:05:19.735 --> 01:05:20.759
The what?


01:05:20.936 --> 01:05:24.099
The entrances to the caves,
they're all underwater.


01:05:24.273 --> 01:05:25.638
How would we get in?


01:05:26.608 --> 01:05:29.008
You're in luck. I rent scuba gear.


01:05:29.244 --> 01:05:31.940
I'll give you a good deal too.


01:05:44.493 --> 01:05:46.484
Smile.


01:06:29.204 --> 01:06:31.399
Zoinks.


01:06:44.019 --> 01:06:45.884
FRED:
Lights.


01:07:04.706 --> 01:07:05.730
Uh-oh.


01:07:13.448 --> 01:07:15.109
VELMA [IN DISTORTED VOICE]:
Ah.


01:07:15.284 --> 01:07:18.310
You've been a faithful servant.


01:07:18.487 --> 01:07:23.447
And now I think you deserve
some playmates.


01:07:23.625 --> 01:07:25.252
[BELLOWS]


01:07:27.362 --> 01:07:29.455
She's making more of those things.


01:07:36.672 --> 01:07:39.163
VELMA:
Rise, my slithering slaves.


01:07:39.408 --> 01:07:42.900
Rise and serve your new master.


01:07:47.983 --> 01:07:50.076
[GROWLING]


01:07:50.452 --> 01:07:51.476
[GASPS]


01:07:51.653 --> 01:07:53.951
Finally, we'll make them pay.


01:07:54.122 --> 01:07:57.614
Make them rue the day
they set foot on our land.


01:07:58.293 --> 01:08:00.818
Those things are gonna attack
everyone in town.


01:08:00.996 --> 01:08:04.124
- We have to do something.
- What can we do?


01:08:04.299 --> 01:08:07.928
Hey, Fred, I know this is usually
your department, but do you mind--?


01:08:08.103 --> 01:08:10.970
- If you've got a plan, Shaggy, go for it.
- Okay.


01:08:12.307 --> 01:08:16.004
Velma Dacey Dinkley,
you stop that this instant.


01:08:17.112 --> 01:08:22.948
I told you,
Velma doesn't live here anymore.


01:08:23.151 --> 01:08:25.619
That was your big idea, Shags?


01:08:25.821 --> 01:08:29.154
Creatures, change of plans.


01:08:29.358 --> 01:08:30.620
Get them.


01:08:31.960 --> 01:08:33.951
SCOOBY:
Hold still.


01:08:37.366 --> 01:08:38.993
Thank you. Aah!


01:08:50.245 --> 01:08:51.303
Velma.


01:08:51.480 --> 01:08:55.211
Velma, I know you're still in there.
I know you can hear me.


01:08:57.219 --> 01:09:00.154
Okay, like, maybe you can't.


01:09:04.793 --> 01:09:06.226
DAPHNE:
This is like biology class...


01:09:06.395 --> 01:09:09.558
...except this time
the frogs are gonna dissect us.


01:09:11.500 --> 01:09:13.730
Like, come on, V.
You gotta listen to me.


01:09:13.902 --> 01:09:16.769
You're stronger than this thing
inside of you.


01:09:17.005 --> 01:09:21.374
You're stronger
and you're smarter and you're cuter.


01:09:22.244 --> 01:09:25.008
- [IN NORMAL VOICE] I am?
- That's right, V.


01:09:25.180 --> 01:09:28.843
I think everything about you is cute.
Like the way...


01:09:29.017 --> 01:09:31.747
...your pleated skirt ruffles
when you run from ghosts.


01:09:31.987 --> 01:09:33.352
How-- And even--


01:09:33.522 --> 01:09:37.686
Even how you lose your glasses
at the most inopportune moments.


01:09:37.859 --> 01:09:43.058
Yeah. Yeah, as a matter of fact,
that might be the cutest thing of all.


01:09:43.999 --> 01:09:45.899
Shaggy?


01:09:46.568 --> 01:09:48.934
- Help me.
- Yeah.


01:09:49.137 --> 01:09:52.197
Yeah, listen, V.
You gotta fight this old witch.


01:09:52.407 --> 01:09:53.431
- Okay.
- Okay?


01:09:53.608 --> 01:09:56.543
Shaggy, I'll try. I'll try.


01:09:56.712 --> 01:09:58.577
[IN DISTORTED VOICE]
No, you won't.


01:09:59.715 --> 01:10:01.546
[SHAGGY SCREAMING]


01:10:05.754 --> 01:10:10.384
Well, at least now I can finally say
I've been picked up by a girl.


01:10:31.913 --> 01:10:34.177
See you, froggies.


01:10:42.991 --> 01:10:45.152
FRED:
Run, run.


01:10:54.836 --> 01:10:57.304
That ought to hold them for a while.
Come on.


01:11:02.477 --> 01:11:04.945
Knock me down all you want,
Wanda Grubwort...


01:11:05.147 --> 01:11:09.709
...but I'm not gonna let a couple of
stupid moonstones take my friend away.


01:11:10.719 --> 01:11:13.085
Oh, wait, moon. Oh, that's it.


01:11:14.022 --> 01:11:17.185
[SINGING]
By the light of the silvery moon


01:11:17.359 --> 01:11:18.519
What is it? What are you--?


01:11:18.693 --> 01:11:20.558
By the light


01:11:20.729 --> 01:11:22.458
[IN NORMAL VOICE]
Not the dark but the light


01:11:23.665 --> 01:11:26.031
Of the silvery moon


01:11:26.201 --> 01:11:28.829
Not the sun, but the moon


01:11:29.004 --> 01:11:30.995
I want to spoon


01:11:31.173 --> 01:11:32.731
[IN DISTORTED VOICE]
No, you're mine.


01:11:32.974 --> 01:11:37.377
- To my honey I'll croon love's tune
- [IN NORMAL VOICE] Croon love's tune


01:11:38.013 --> 01:11:42.882
- Oh, by the light of the silvery
- Light of the silvery


01:11:43.385 --> 01:11:45.876
VELMA: Moon
WANDA: Oh!


01:11:46.054 --> 01:11:47.646
[GROANING]


01:11:55.363 --> 01:11:56.489
It's a dead end.


01:12:00.168 --> 01:12:02.193
I'm sorry, Daph.


01:12:02.370 --> 01:12:03.928
I really was a jerk.


01:12:04.172 --> 01:12:05.935
I'm sorry too, Fred.


01:12:06.141 --> 01:12:09.167
I never should've tried
to make you jealous.


01:12:10.078 --> 01:12:12.273
[MONSTERS ROARING]


01:12:13.782 --> 01:12:18.719
Get out of me, Wanda Grubwort.


01:12:21.756 --> 01:12:23.849
[WANDA SCREAMING]


01:12:28.263 --> 01:12:32.757
Nothing can stop me now. Come.


01:12:48.116 --> 01:12:50.084
SCOOBY:
Not so fast.


01:12:50.285 --> 01:12:52.048
What? No.


01:12:52.621 --> 01:12:55.920
Say goodbye, wicked witch.


01:12:56.124 --> 01:13:01.152
No, no. Revenge was in my grasp.


01:13:01.329 --> 01:13:03.729
And I would have gotten away
with it...


01:13:03.899 --> 01:13:08.734
...if it wasn't for you meddling kids
and your rotten dog.


01:13:08.904 --> 01:13:09.928
[GIGGLES]


01:13:10.105 --> 01:13:14.201
Oh, no. No.


01:13:15.243 --> 01:13:17.108
[SCREAMS]


01:13:18.013 --> 01:13:20.106
[MONSTERS SLITHERING]


01:13:25.820 --> 01:13:27.287
[FROGS CROAKING]


01:13:31.092 --> 01:13:33.583
Shaggy did it. Come on.


01:13:35.297 --> 01:13:37.128
VELMA:
Shaggy?


01:13:38.500 --> 01:13:40.365
Is it over?


01:13:44.472 --> 01:13:46.838
I think so, V.


01:13:49.010 --> 01:13:51.171
Those things you said to me.


01:13:53.114 --> 01:13:54.775
Did you really mean all of that?


01:13:55.884 --> 01:13:57.943
Of course I did.


01:13:58.153 --> 01:14:01.486
I've been trying to say it
ever since we got here.


01:14:04.125 --> 01:14:06.252
Just kiss her already.


01:14:06.761 --> 01:14:09.025
Oh, well, I--


01:14:09.264 --> 01:14:11.789
Shaggy, just kiss me already.


01:14:22.277 --> 01:14:23.744
SHAGGY:
Well, um....


01:14:23.912 --> 01:14:25.539
That was, uh....


01:14:26.381 --> 01:14:27.780
Yeah.


01:14:28.817 --> 01:14:32.150
You know,
I don't know too much about chemistry.


01:14:32.320 --> 01:14:34.220
I do, Shaggy.


01:14:34.422 --> 01:14:39.826
And, well, there just wasn't any.


01:14:39.995 --> 01:14:42.020
Yeah, I....


01:14:42.831 --> 01:14:47.165
You know, maybe we're just better off
being friends.


01:14:47.335 --> 01:14:49.895
You know what? Maybe we all are.


01:14:50.071 --> 01:14:51.561
Yeah.


01:14:52.574 --> 01:14:53.871
Phew.


01:14:54.042 --> 01:14:57.705
THORNY: Well, kids, with the creature
gone, we have a ton of new applications.


01:14:57.879 --> 01:14:59.608
Maybe more than we can handle.


01:15:00.248 --> 01:15:02.842
- And it's all thanks to you guys.
- Aw.


01:15:05.520 --> 01:15:08.250
Oh, that reminds me.


01:15:10.859 --> 01:15:15.353
FRED: What?
- Something to show my appreciation.


01:15:15.530 --> 01:15:18.397
- Ten thousand dollars?
- Uncle Thorny.


01:15:18.566 --> 01:15:20.193
- Oh.
- Aw.


01:15:22.470 --> 01:15:26.099
By the way, I took the liberty to set up
an appointment with my attorney...


01:15:26.274 --> 01:15:28.037
...for you to discuss incorporating.


01:15:28.710 --> 01:15:31.543
Thought that might help
with your future liability issues.


01:15:31.713 --> 01:15:33.112
- Yeah.
- Oh, man.


01:15:33.281 --> 01:15:36.148
- Shall we go play around?
SHAGGY: This is gonna be amazing, guys.


01:15:36.351 --> 01:15:38.876
- So insane.
- Hey, you guys, I've got it.


01:15:39.054 --> 01:15:41.284
We can be Mystery Incorporated.


01:15:41.456 --> 01:15:43.481
- I love it.
- I can totally dig that.


01:15:43.658 --> 01:15:45.057
Hey, Scooby, get a picture.


01:15:45.260 --> 01:15:46.591
[LAUGHS]


01:15:46.761 --> 01:15:48.160
FRED:
Everybody say, "Mystery Inc."


01:15:48.396 --> 01:15:50.796
ALL:
Mystery Inc.


01:15:50.965 --> 01:15:53.058
- Oh, my goodness.
- Guys, group hug.


01:15:53.234 --> 01:15:55.099
- Okay.
- Okay, all right.


01:15:55.270 --> 01:15:57.101
VELMA: Okay, Shaggy.
DAPHNE: Shaggy.


01:15:57.272 --> 01:15:59.638
VELMA: Shaggy.
FRED: Okay....


01:16:00.975 --> 01:16:03.307
All right. We'll celebrate.


01:16:03.511 --> 01:16:04.569
All right. Bye, guys.


01:16:04.746 --> 01:16:07.146
Not the hair, man. Not the hair.


01:16:08.316 --> 01:16:09.442
[SIGHS]


01:16:10.652 --> 01:16:12.313
[WHIMPERING]


01:16:12.487 --> 01:16:14.580
[GRUNTING]


01:16:28.269 --> 01:16:29.293
Don't worry, Scoob.


01:16:30.004 --> 01:16:33.838
No matter what happens,
I'll always be here for you.


01:16:34.042 --> 01:16:36.636
Oh, Shaggy.


01:16:49.290 --> 01:16:51.383
[SINGING]
When danger used to come around


01:16:51.559 --> 01:16:53.618
I would fall right to the ground


01:16:53.795 --> 01:16:56.025
It's true


01:16:58.166 --> 01:17:01.192
But now that I can see your face


01:17:01.369 --> 01:17:06.238
Well, I can stand up to anything


01:17:06.441 --> 01:17:09.205
And how I cherish the times


01:17:09.377 --> 01:17:14.144
When the sun shines on the two of us


01:17:14.549 --> 01:17:16.016
But I don't mind going through


01:17:16.184 --> 01:17:21.520
The bad times
Just as long as they're with you


01:17:22.090 --> 01:17:25.526
Well, I can be scared with you


01:17:26.661 --> 01:17:29.027
I can be alone with you


01:17:30.465 --> 01:17:34.731
As long as I have your hand
To hold onto


01:17:34.903 --> 01:17:40.239
I can be scared with you


01:17:40.408 --> 01:17:43.070
[CHORUS HUMMING]


01:17:46.247 --> 01:17:50.115
I can be scared with you


01:17:50.285 --> 01:17:55.780
Oh, I can be scared
As long as I'm with you


01:17:58.593 --> 01:18:02.620
I can do anything


01:18:02.797 --> 01:18:05.925
I can do anything


01:18:06.100 --> 01:18:11.902
As long as I'm with you


01:18:12.307 --> 01:18:14.400
[DISCO MUSIC PLAYING]


01:18:27.088 --> 01:18:29.522
[SINGING]
I can be scared with you


01:18:31.226 --> 01:18:33.558
I can be alone with you


01:18:35.063 --> 01:18:37.554
I can be scared with you


01:18:38.733 --> 01:18:41.566
As long as I'm with you


01:18:43.271 --> 01:18:45.296
My name is Shaggy
I like to eat


01:18:45.540 --> 01:18:47.167
Main man Scooby
But he got four feet


01:18:47.408 --> 01:18:50.400
Me and my homeys solve mysteries
Through cartoons, movies


01:18:50.578 --> 01:18:51.602
And tons of DVDs


01:18:51.779 --> 01:18:55.340
As old school goes, we're genuine
We've been kicking it since 1969


01:18:55.583 --> 01:18:57.448
But Mystery Inc. is far from through


01:18:57.619 --> 01:19:00.611
Because there's always more adventures
Starring me Scooby-Doo


01:19:18.573 --> 01:19:21.633
Scooby-Dooby-Doo.

